Z||000000||fieroshop||05-10-2000||09:37 PM||||Well I went out today and piched out the green color that we are going to use on my 88 GT. The first thing i did was get sticker shock from the price of the paint. Then I had my painter test pait a small metal can to check out the color. The color I am doing is a dark forest green metallic as a base coat which is applied over black primer. Next we are going to paint three coats of clear with perl in the paint and finally three more coats of clear with nothing in it. So far several of my customers have seen it and are all drooling over the color. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||05-10-2000||10:16 PM||||We had a Forest Green GT and a Notchback at a Monterey Western Regional. They look real good!||||reg||6
Z||000002||pollock||05-11-2000||02:15 PM||||My dad's 86GT is Forest Green.  Beautiful.||||reg||10
Z||000003||ChadMan||05-11-2000||02:52 PM||||There's a guy (from PA, I think) who has a medium green metallic fastback GT with the stock pewter aero cladding.  It is beautiful and unique - not a dark British green, but certainly not a tacky mint green like you see on Geos and Hyundais.<P>Every year he comes to the Nationals, every year I take a picture of his car, and every year the photos don't do the color justice!<P>Has anybody else seen this car?||||reg||14
